    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d715">

                <pb facs="0975" n="965" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg965"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00)119 Control (Germany)/9–2245:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Political Adviser for Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Murphy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frankfurt</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-09-22">September 22,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received September 22—12:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>62. USFET (United States Forces European Theater) has ordered the reorganization
                    of the US western military district into two German states (Laender) to include
                    respectively a Land Wurttemberg-Baden as already set up, and a new Land of
                    “Greater Hessen”.<anchor n="91" xml:id="d715-f1"/> See our despatch 519 June
                        30.<anchor n="92" xml:id="d715-f2"/> Land Greater Hessen includes former
                    Land Hessen and US portions of provinces of Kurhessen and Nassau. G–5
                    representative has announced that no city has yet been selected as capital of
                    Land Greater Hessen but several possibilities are being studied. He also
                    indicated that a civilian administrative president for the area will be named
                    shortly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Murphy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d715-f1" n="91" xml:id="d715-f1-content">
                <p>Text of Proclamation No. 2 by General Eisenhower, September 19, 1945, setting up
                    the three states of Greater Hessen, Württemberg-Baden, and Bavaria, is printed
                    in Pollock and Meisel, <hi rendition="#italic">Germany Under Occupation</hi>, p.
                    119.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d715-f2" n="92" xml:id="d715-f2-content">
